Fixes "Please specify gift card amount" when adding a gift card with a predefined amount to the cart (aheadworks/module-giftcard 1.10.4).

Root cause: 1.10.4 resolves the paid price of a predefined amount through lookupPaidAmount(), which returns the
discounted price ("custom_price") of the matching amount row even when it is empty. Amount rows without a discounted
price store custom_price as NULL, so the resolved amount becomes null and validation rejects the buy request.
Up to 1.10.3 the isset() check skipped such rows and the face value was used.
Fix: use the discounted price only when it is numeric, otherwise fall back to the face value.

diff --git a/Model/Product/Type/Giftcard.php b/Model/Product/Type/Giftcard.php
index 82c1c9c..5eeb542 100644
--- a/Model/Product/Type/Giftcard.php
+++ b/Model/Product/Type/Giftcard.php
@@ -733,7 +733,10 @@ class Giftcard extends AbstractType
     private function lookupPaidAmount($face, array $discountPrices)
     {
         foreach ($discountPrices as $mappedFace => $paid) {
-            if (is_numeric($mappedFace) && abs((float)$mappedFace - (float)$face) < 0.00001) {
+            // BEGIN PATCH
+            // if (is_numeric($mappedFace) && abs((float)$mappedFace - (float)$face) < 0.00001) {
+            if (is_numeric($mappedFace) && abs((float)$mappedFace - (float)$face) < 0.00001 && is_numeric($paid)) {
+            // END PATCH
                 return $paid;
             }
         }
